# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AdFund Global — CRM (Next.js) environment
# Copy to `.env` for local development.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Backend origin. REQUIRED in every deployed environment.
#
# Used by two things:
#   1. next.config.ts rewrites() — proxies /api/* to the API so the auth
#      cookie is first-party. This is what makes login work in production.
#   2. Server Components calling the API directly during SSR.
#
# Format: scheme + host only. No trailing slash, and no /api/v1 suffix —
# the rewrite appends the path itself.
#   good: https://api.example.com
#   bad:  https://api.example.com/        (trailing slash)
#   bad:  https://api.example.com/api/v1  (path included)
#
# On Vercel this must be set under Settings → Environment Variables for every
# environment you deploy (Production, Preview, Development). It is read at
# BUILD time by rewrites(), so the build fails with a clear message rather
# than silently baking in localhost.
#
# Server-only (no NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix), so it never reaches the browser.
API_ORIGIN=http://localhost:8000

# Optional. Browser-side base path for API calls; defaults to "/api/v1",
# which routes through the rewrite above. Only override if you are
# deliberately bypassing the proxy — that reintroduces the cross-origin
# cookie problem where you appear logged in but every request 401s.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_PATH=/api/v1
